.github.com/users/sigmund68k/following{/other_user}","gists_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sigmund68k/gists{/gist_id}","starred_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sigmund68k/starred{/owner}{/repo}","subscriptions_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sigmund68k/subscriptions","organizations_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sigmund68k/orgs","repos_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sigmund68k/repos","events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sigmund68k/events{/privacy}","received_events_url":"https://api.github.com/users/sigmund68k/received_events","type":"User","user_view_type":"public","site_admin":false},"created_at":"2026-01-14T16:53:14Z","updated_at":"2026-01-14T16:53:14Z","body":"I've stripped down the MRP to a simpler project, and attached.  \n[sm-visible-error.zip](https://github.com/user-attachments/files/24619513/sm-visible-error.zip)\n\nThis includes two test classes.  Child1 is the parent, and contains only a VisibilityEnabler2D.  Child2 is the child, and adds an AudioStreamPlayer2D.  Instantiating Child2 triggers the same error.\n\nI don't believe this is directly tied to the inheritance relationship, rather the VisibilityEnabler2D disabling the entire class before _ready is called on AudioStreamPlayer2D.  I have been able to reproduce this with simpler classes with ordering, as seen in https://github.com/godotengine/godot/issues/112477.\n\nI actually ran into this by accidentally nesting two enemy scenes in my game that have VisibilityEnabler2D and AudioStreamPlayer2D.  So it can be caused by composition as well.\n\nCurrently looking in Node2D in C++, catching in VS.","author_association":"CONTRIBUTOR","pin":null,"reactions":{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3750528459/reactions","total_count":2,"+1":1,"-1":0,"laugh":0,"hooray":0,"confused":0,"heart":0,"rocket":0,"eyes":1},"performed_via_github_app":null,"minimized":null},{"url":"https://api.github.com/repos/godotengine/godot/issues/comments/3750863737","html_url"